Unofficial LocalSend protocol client for Windows XP SP3 and later.
Distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

This product includes software developed by the OpenSSL Project for use in the
OpenSSL Toolkit (http://www.openssl.org/).  The binary release bundles the
OpenSSL 1.0.2u runtime libraries (libeay32.dll, ssleay32.dll), which are
distributed under the OpenSSL License and the original SSLeay License; both are
BSD style licenses.  The full texts ship as licenses\LICENSE-OpenSSL.txt and in
installer\licenses\LICENSE-OpenSSL.txt.

The binary release also contains a bundle of root certificates taken from the
Mozilla CA certificate store (certs\ca-bundle.crt, as redistributed by the curl
project at https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html), which is distributed under the
Mozilla Public License 2.0.  It is used to verify HTTPS peers on systems whose
own root certificate store is out of date, such as Windows XP SP3.

LocalSendXP implements the LocalSend protocol, which is documented at
https://github.com/localsend/protocol.  This project is not affiliated with the
official LocalSend project.
